 "output" : "The pasted lift feature files had real integration bugs, not backend incompatibility — the backend itself was fine. Here's what was wrong and what I did:

Root causes found:

Missing npm deps (MUI, formik, yup, notistack, dayjs, axios, react-router-dom) — package.json only had react/react-dom.
Missing shared infra the files assumed existed: src/api/*, src/utils/*, src/components/*, src/theme/*, src/context/AuthContext — none existed.
Broken relative paths — Lifts.jsx and LiftSelect.jsx were one level off (missing a ../), and Lifts.jsx self-referenced ./lifts/LiftFormDialog from inside the lifts/ folder it's already in.
A typo bug: @mui/icons-material/DeleteOutline (doesn't exist) vs. the correct DeleteOutlined.
Nothing mounted <Lifts/> — Workspace.jsx just showed placeholder text.
LiftDetailDialog depends on Scheduling/Inspections/Defects/Rectifications APIs that don't exist on the backend yet.
What I did:

Installed the missing deps, pinned MUI to ^6/@mui/x-data-grid@^7 (the latest tag resolved to a much newer major that broke Stack/Grid — pinning removed console warnings entirely).
Built out src/api/{client,liftApi,scheduleApi,inspectionApi,defectApi,rectificationApi}.js, src/utils/{formatDate,csvExport,liftHelpers}.js, src/components/{StatCard,StatusChip,ConfirmDialog}.jsx, src/theme/statusColors.js, src/context/AuthContext.jsx (stub Admin user, since there's no login system yet).
Fixed all the broken import paths and the icon typo; made LiftDetailDialog's cross-module fetches fail gracefully (empty lists) since those backend routes aren't mounted yet, and fixed a /schedules vs /scheduling route-name mismatch.
Added real routing (BrowserRouter + SnackbarProvider + AuthProvider in main.jsx, URL-driven tabs in App.jsx), and mounted <Lifts/> in Workspace.jsx.
Backend fix: found and fixed a real bug — creating/updating a lift with a duplicate liftCode threw a raw Mongo error → 500, instead of a clean message. Now returns 400 "Lift code ... already exists", which the frontend's snackbar already handles.
Verified live, not just by reading code: spun up a throwaway in-memory MongoDB, ran the real backend against it, and drove the actual UI in headless Chromium — list/stats load, Add Lift dialog creates a lift end-to-end, grid and stat cards update, zero console errors, zero failed requests. All temporary test infra (test Mongo, test server instances) has been torn down; your real MongoDB service was left untouched.

One thing I couldn't verify: your actual backend/.env doesn't have DATABASE_URL set (no .env file exists yet, only .env.example), so I can't confirm the app against your real Atlas cluster — you'll need to create backend/.env with your real connection string."
